   "label": "Atmosphere",
   "quote": "iam die labente",
   "trans": "as the day was now fading",
   "body": "A quiet ablative absolute sets the scene: <em>iam die labente</em>, \"with the day now slipping away\". The fading light mirrors Psyche’s exhaustion and the gathering gloom of her fortunes as she stumbles, lost, towards the sisters’ city.",
   "exam": "<strong>In an exam:</strong> \"The ablative absolute <em>iam die labente</em> lends atmosphere: the dying daylight matches Psyche’s weary, friendless wandering and lends a sombre tone to her arrival at the very city of a treacherous sister.\"",
   "line": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "mentito-nomine",
   "cat": "diction",
   "label": "Loaded Diction",
   "quote": "mariti mentito nomine",
   "trans": "under the false name of husband",
   "body": "Psyche repeats the sisters’ lie back to them: the \"beast\" had slept with her <em>mariti mentito nomine</em> — \"under the lying name of husband\". The phrase drips with the deception she has swallowed, and dramatic irony: the \"beast\" was her true, divine husband.",
   "exam": "<strong>In an exam:</strong> \"The phrase <em>mariti mentito nomine</em> shows Psyche parroting the sisters’ slander; the dramatic irony is sharp — the ‘false husband’ was in fact the god Cupid, her real and loving spouse.\"",
   "line": ""
