   "label": "Monstrous Imagery",
   "quote": "ingluvie voraci me misellam hauriret",
   "trans": "(before) he could gulp down poor little me with his ravenous throat",
   "body": "The sisters’ invented monster looms here: a <em>vorax ingluvies</em> (\"ravenous gullet\") about to <em>haurire</em> (\"gulp down\") Psyche whole. The cannibal imagery makes vivid the lie she believed — and the horror she was driven to.",
   "exam": "<strong>In an exam:</strong> \"The cannibalistic imagery of the <em>vorax ingluvies</em> that would <em>haurire</em> her conveys the monstrous lie the sisters planted, justifying (in Psyche’s retelling) the murderous plan she nearly carried out.\"",
